cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use DispatchAtlas in your research, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
title: DispatchAtlas
abstract: >-
  DispatchAtlas is a Python library for reproducible benchmarking of
  scheduling algorithms. One data model covers machine scheduling,
  resource-constrained project scheduling, and the placement of tasks across
  an edge-fog-cloud continuum. Benchmark families generate problems from a
  seed, and published suites are rebuilt exactly or read from their files.
  Heuristics, metaheuristics, multi-objective, learning, and exact solvers
  share one contract that enforces stop criteria and counts evaluations
  exactly. Campaigns run every solver on every problem with paired seeds,
  record each run, resume after interruptions, and replay runs to verify that
  they reproduce, and the analysis reports non-parametric tests with effect
  sizes and confidence intervals, quality indicators, tables, and figures.
authors:
